    <briefdescription>
<para>An enumeration of various forms of method existence: </para>
<para>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Implied</bold> - the method exists implicitly; this is the result of the <javadoccode>into</javadoccode> clause, or the methods of <javadoccode>Object</javadoccode> in the context of an interface, for example; </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Interface</bold> - the method is defined as part of an interface; </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Class</bold> - the method is defined as part of a class. </para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Only the highest level of existence is used; for example, a method that exists due to an &quot;into type&quot; clause, an &quot;implements interface&quot; clause, and is also implemented on a class, is considered to have an <ref refid="df/d62/enumorg_1_1xvm_1_1asm_1_1constants_1_1_method_body_1_1_existence" kindref="compound">Existence</ref> of &quot;Class&quot;. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
